══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SECTION 2 — PROBLEM STATEMENT
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Students frequently struggle to locate specific information buried across
  lengthy course materials such as lecture notes, syllabi, and reference
  textbooks. Traditional keyword-based search is inadequate for nuanced academic
  queries, and manually reviewing entire documents is extremely time-consuming.

  This project addresses the challenge by providing a Retrieval-Augmented
  Generation (RAG) based conversational study assistant that allows students to
  query their own uploaded PDF documents in natural language and receive accurate,
  context-grounded answers strictly derived from the source material — not
  invented by the model.

  The system is specifically designed to minimize hallucination by:
    •  Only calling the LLM when relevant context is successfully retrieved
    •  Instructing the LLM via system prompt to use only retrieved context
    •  Providing source citations (document name + page number) with every answer
    •  Returning an explicit fallback message when no relevant content is found


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━


══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SECTION 3 — TARGET USERS / USE CASE
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  PRIMARY TARGET USERS
  ─────────────────────
    •  Undergraduate and postgraduate students studying from PDF-based course
       materials (lecture slides, textbooks, syllabi, handouts)
    •  Self-learners who need a personalized, interactive interface to their
       study documents

  PRACTICAL USE CASE
  ───────────────────
    A student uploads one or more PDF files — for example, a Database Management
    textbook or Operating Systems lecture notes — and interacts with the assistant
    through a chat interface to:

      →  Ask specific conceptual questions from their notes
      →  Generate custom multiple-choice practice quizzes on any topic
      →  Create flashcard decks for key terms and definitions
      →  Get structured revision summaries for any chapter or topic

    All outputs are grounded strictly in the student's own uploaded materials.


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━


══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SECTION 4 — WHAT THE GENAI SYSTEM WILL DO
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The GenAI component performs five core functions:

  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  FUNCTION 1 — RAG Question Answering (Chat)                               │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  The student types a question. The system converts it into a semantic      │
  │  embedding vector, retrieves the top-K most relevant chunks from the       │
  │  vector database, constructs a grounded prompt, and sends it to the LLM.  │
  │  The LLM generates an answer using only the retrieved context. If no       │
  │  relevant context is found, the LLM is not called — a fallback message     │
  │  is returned instead.                                                      │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  FUNCTION 2 — Practice Quiz Generation                                    │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  Given a topic, the system retrieves related content from the vector       │
  │  store and instructs the LLM to generate Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)  │
  │  in a structured JSON format. The student can take the quiz interactively  │
  │  and receive an automatic score.                                           │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  FUNCTION 3 — Flashcard Creation                                          │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  For a given topic, the system retrieves relevant document chunks and       │
  │  prompts the LLM to generate study flashcards (front: term / question,     │
  │  back: definition / answer) in JSON format, displayed interactively.       │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  FUNCTION 4 — Topic Summary / Revision Guide                              │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  The system retrieves up to 8 relevant chunks for an entered topic and     │
  │  prompts the LLM to produce a structured revision guide with a summary     │
  │  paragraph and bullet-point key takeaways.                                 │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  FUNCTION 5 — Source-Cited Answers                                        │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  Every chat answer includes expandable source citations showing the exact  │
  │  document filename and page number from which each piece of information    │
  │  was retrieved, enabling students to verify answers against originals.     │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


