══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SECTION 8 — ONE THING I AM CURRENTLY UNSURE ABOUT
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  UNCERTAINTY: Reliable LLM JSON Output Parsing for Quizzes and Flashcards

  The quiz and flashcard generation features depend on the LLM returning a
  strictly valid JSON array in a prescribed format. A cleanup helper function
  (_clean_json_output) has been implemented to strip markdown code fences that
  LLMs sometimes include around JSON. However, it is currently uncertain whether
  this approach is robust enough across all supported LLM providers and model
  sizes.

  Specifically:
    •  Smaller local models (e.g., gemma, mistral via Ollama) may still return
       malformed or inconsistently structured JSON, causing json.loads() to fail
    •  Different models may output extra commentary text before or after the JSON
    •  There is no retry-with-correction loop if parsing fails

  A more reliable solution — such as LangChain's with_structured_output() using
  Pydantic models — may be needed for consistent production-grade behavior, but
  its compatibility and behavior across all three supported providers (Groq,
  OpenAI, Ollama) has not been fully evaluated yet.


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━


