══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  PROJECT SUMMARY
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  StudyRAG is a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) powered study assistant
  built as a fully interactive Streamlit web application. It solves the problem
  of students being unable to efficiently locate and use specific information
  from lengthy PDF study materials by allowing them to chat with their documents
  in natural language. The system uses LangChain to orchestrate a pipeline that
  embeds uploaded PDFs into a local vector database (FAISS or ChromaDB),
  retrieves the most relevant text chunks for any user query, and then uses a
  configurable LLM (Groq, OpenAI, or local Ollama) to generate accurate,
  citation-backed answers. Beyond Q&A, the same RAG pipeline automatically
  generates graded practice quizzes, study flashcards, and structured topic
  summaries from the student's own course materials — making it a comprehensive
  AI study companion that benefits all students seeking a smarter way to study.


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━


